['Your request involves a wide range of complex programming tasks, including dynamic loading of libraries, managing dependencies, concurrent access, and comprehensive testing. Implementing all these features will be quite extensive and may not be possible within the scope of this text-based interface. Moreover, providing code blocks for each feature individually would not result in a complete system.

Here is an outline of the general approach to implement such a cryptographic module manager:
```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <dlfcn.h>
#include <pthread.h>

typedef void* (*create_fn)(void);
typedef void  (*destroy_fn)(void*);
typedef char* (*get_name_fn)(void);

typedef struct {
    void* handle;
    create_fn create;
    destroy_fn destroy;
    get_name_fn get_name;
} CryptoPlugin;

CryptoPlugin* plugins[3];  // You can add more as per your need.
pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

void load_plugins() {
    const char* libs[] = {"lib1", "lib2", "lib3"};  // Add your library names here

    for(int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
        void* handle = dlopen(libs[i], RTLD_LAZY);

        if(!handle) {
            fprintf(stderr, "Cannot load library: %s\n", dlerror());
            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
        }

        plugins[i]->create = (create_fn)dlsym(handle, "create");
        plugins[i]->destroy = (destroy_fn)dlsym(handle, "destroy");
        plugins[i]->get_name = (get_name_fn)dlsym(handle, "get_name");

        char* error;
        if((error = dlerror()) != NULL) {
            fprintf(stderr, "%s\n", error);
            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
        }
    }
}

void crypto_function() {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    // Use the plugin functions here. For example:
    for(int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
        void* obj = plugins[i]->create();

        printf("Plugin name: %s\n", plugins[i]->get_name());

        plugins[i]->destroy(obj);
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}

int main() {
    load_plugins();
    crypto_function();

    return 0;
}
```
Please note this is just an outline and does not cover all aspects of your request. It's assumed that the external libraries will have "create", "destroy" and "get_name" functions. You might need to implement a custom error handling mechanism, logging, and concurrent access control as per your requirements.
']

