        return defaultThemeDirectory;
    }

    @Override
    public void setDefaultTheme(String themePath) { /* Not applicable */ }
}
```
4. Implement a class `CompositeThemeCache` that chains together multiple ThemeCache instances:
```java
class CompositeThemeCache implements ThemeCache {
    private final List<ThemeCache> caches;

    public CompositeThemeCache(List<ThemeCache> caches) {
        this.caches = caches;
    }

    @Override
    public String getDefaultThemeDirectory() {
        for (ThemeCache cache : caches) {
            String themePath = cache.getDefaultThemeDirectory();
            if (themePath != null) {
                return themePath;
            }
        }
        // Fallback mechanism here
    }

    @Override
    public void setDefaultTheme(String themePath) { /* Not applicable */ }
}
```
5. Implement a factory that returns either the `FileSystemThemeCache` or `CompositeThemeCache`, depending on whether there's network:
```java
class ThemeCacheFactory {
    public static ThemeCache create(ConfigurationService configService) {
        if (NetworkChecker.isNetworkAvailable()) {
            return new CompositeThemeCache(Arrays.asList(new NetworkThemeCache(configService), new FileSystemThemeCache("default")));
        } else {
            return new FileSystemThemeCache("default");
        }
    }
}
```
6. Use the theme cache:
