import asyncio
from abc import ABC, abstractmethod
from typing import Any, List

# Abstract class for different protocols
class Protocol(ABC):
    @abstractmethod
    def send(self, message: Any) -> None:
        pass

    @abstractmethod
    def receive(self) -> Any:
        pass


# Concrete classes implementing the abstract methods for different protocols
class AMQPProtocol(Protocol):
    # Implement abstract methods here...


class MQTTProtocol(Protocol):
    # Implement abstract methods here...


class KafkaProtocol(Protocol):
    # Implement abstract methods here...


# The main class for the messaging system
class MessagingSystem:
    def __init__(self, protocols: List[Protocol]):
        self.protocols = protocols

    async def send_message(self, message: Any) -> None:
        for protocol in self.protocols:
            await protocol.send(message)

    async def receive_message(self) -> Any:
        results = await asyncio.gather(*[protocol.receive() for protocol in self.protocols])
        return [result for result in results if result is not None]
```

This code provides a skeleton structure to start with. You can extend the `Protocol` class and implement different protocols, like AMQP, MQTT, or Kafka. The `MessagingSystem` uses these protocols to send and receive messages. Note that this is a simplified version and does not include many of the features you requested such as user authentication, resource management, logging/monitoring, etc. These are all complex topics on their own and would require significant additional code.

