```javascript
function createDynamicForm(fields, config = {}) {
    const form = document.createElement('form');

    fields.forEach((field) => {
        const element = document.createElement(field.type);

        if (field.attributes) {
            Object.keys(field.attributes).forEach(key => {
                element[key] = field.attributes[key];
            });
        }

        form.appendChild(element);
    });

    return form;
}
```
This function receives an array of fields where each field is an object that represents a form input (text, select, radio...). It creates the corresponding HTML element and adds it to the form. 

