["This is a high level task and requires a complete development cycle with multiple components that cannot be demonstrated through a single function or snippet of code. However, I can help you understand how such system could look like by creating a skeleton for your application using NodeJS and Redis as an example of distributed key-value store and caching service:

```javascript
const redis = require('redis');
const asyncRedisClient = redis.createClient();

class State {
  constructor(id, nextState) {
    this.id = id;
    this.nextState = nextState || null;
  }
}

// Linked List of States
class StateList {
  constructor() {
    this.head = null;
    this.tail = null;
  }

  add(state) {
    if (!this.head) {
      this.head = state;
      this.tail = state;
    } else {
      this.tail.nextState = state;
      this.tail = state;
    }
  }
}

// Finite State Automaton (FSA) object
class FSA {
  constructor(states) {
    this.currentState = states.head;
  }

  async transition() {
    // Lock the current state to prevent concurrent writes
    const lockKey = `lock:${this.currentState.id}`;
    const locked = await asyncRedisClient.setnx(lockKey, '1');
    if (!locked) throw new Error('Failed to acquire lock for the current state');

    // Transition logic here...
    console.log(`Transitioning from ${this.currentState.id} to ${nextState.id}`);

    // Update the FSA's current state and cache it in Redis with a TTL for auto-eviction
    this.currentState = nextState;
    await asyncRedisClient.set(this.currentState.id, JSON.stringify(nextState), 'EX', 60); // Cache for 1 minute

    // Release the lock after transitioning to allow other processes to access the state
    await asyncRedisClient.del(lockKey);
  }
}
```
This is a very basic example and doesn't include many aspects mentioned in your task, such as detailed error handling or logging strategies, memory allocation optimizations, network partition and node failure handling, or graceful shutdown mechanisms for cleanup. You need to extend it based on your specific use cases and requirements. For the complete implementation, you would also require to handle tasks like setting up database connections, integrating with external services, implementing error handling, and developing comprehensive logging and monitoring mechanism. Also consider using libraries or frameworks that can help manage complex state transitions, such as XState or RxJS for reactive programming in JavaScript.
