['Implementing such a complex service in C# would require substantial amount of code that involves multiple classes, libraries, and architectural decisions based on specific requirements like whether to use an HSM or not. 

Below is a simplified example to showcase some key parts of the code. It doesn't cover all the features you requested but can provide a starting point:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.IO;
using System.Text;

public class DynamicSecureEncryptionService : IDisposable
{
    private readonly Aes _aesAlgorithm;
    private bool _disposed = false;

    public DynamicSecureEncryptionService(string key)  // Key could be a parameter from an external KMS
    {
        if (key == null) throw new ArgumentNullException("Key can not be null");

        var keyBytes = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(key);

        _aesAlgorithm = Aes.Create();
        _aesAlgorithm.Mode = CipherMode.CBC;  // or any other mode
        _aesAlgorithm.Key = keyBytes;
    }

    public byte[] Encrypt(byte[] dataToEncrypt)
    {
        return PerformCryptoTransform(_aesAlgorithm.CreateEncryptor(), dataToEncrypt);
    }

    public byte[] Decrypt(byte[] encryptedData)
    {
        return PerformCryptoTransform(_aesAlgorithm.CreateDecryptor(), encryptedData);
    }

    private static byte[] PerformCryptoTransform(ICryptoTransform transform, byte[] data)
    {
        using var memoryStream = new MemoryStream();
        using var cryptoStream = new CryptoStream(memoryStream, transform, CryptoStreamMode.Write);

        cryptoStream.Write(data, 0, data.Length);
        cryptoStream.FlushFinalBlock();

        return memoryStream.ToArray();
    }

    protected virtual void Dispose(bool disposing)
    {
        if (!_disposed && disposing)
            _aesAlgorithm?.Dispose();

        _disposed = true;
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        // Do not change this code. Put cleanup code in 'Dispose(bool disposing)' method
        Dispose(true);
        GC.SuppressFinalize(this);
    }
}
```
This code doesn't cover everything you mentioned like integrating with KMS, handling streaming data and exception handling but hopefully gives a starting point. For concurrency, logging and other features, more complex solutions would be needed which would require multiple classes and possibly third party libraries to handle specific tasks. 

Moreover, please note that working with security is complex and requires careful handling especially when dealing with encryption keys. If you're not experienced in this area, consider consulting with a professional or someone experienced in secure programming practices.
