3. JSON-Avro Conversion:
```java
import org.apache.avro.Schema;
import org.apache.avro.generic.GenericData;
import org.json.JSONObject;

public void jsonToAvro(String json, Schema schema) {
    GenericData.Record record = new GenericData.Record(schema);
    JSONObject jsonObj = new JSONObject(json);

    for (Schema.Field field : schema.getFields()) {
        String fieldName = field.name();
        if (!jsonObj.has(fieldName)) {
            continue; // skip missing fields
        }

        Object jsonValue = jsonObj.opt(fieldName);
        record.put(fieldName, jsonToAvroValue(jsonValue, field.schema()));
    }

    return record;
}
```
This method converts a JSON string to an Avro object given the schema of the destination class. It assumes that the JSON and Avro schemas are compatible.

