["This task involves multiple complex components, including thread safety, multi-threading, error handling, efficient RNG generation, parsing, and LLVM IR code generation. Here is an outline of what the code could look like in Rust:

Firstly, we need to create a random number generator service with thread local storage:
```rust
use rand::{Rng, SeedableRng};
use std::cell::RefCell;
use std::thread;

pub struct RandomNumberService {
    seed: RefCell<u64>,
}

impl RandomNumberService {
    fn new(seed: u64) -> Self {
        let service = Self {
            seed: RefCell::new(seed),
        };

        // Initialize the thread local storage with a unique seed.
        THREAD_LOCAL.with(|tls| {
            *tls.borrow_mut() = rand::thread_rng();
        });

        service
    }

    fn get_random(&self) -> u64 {
        let rng: &mut StdRng = THREAD_LOCAL.with(|tls| tls);
        let seed = self.seed.borrow();

        // Generate a random number with the unique seed for each thread.
        *rng = SeedableRng::seed_from_u64(*seed);
        rng.gen()
    }
}
```
Note: The RNG service in this code does not support multi-threaded operations and managing a single instance throughout the application’s lifecycle yet, you can add them according to your needs. 

Next, we will create an LLVM IR generator function:
```rust
use std::fs;
use llvm_sys::LLVMInitializeNativeTarget;
use lexer::{Lexer, Token};
use parser::Parser;
use codegen::CodeGen;

pub fn generate_llvm_ir(file_path: &str) {
    LLVMInitializeNativeTarget(); // Initialize the native target for LLVM.

    let file = fs::read_to_string(file_path).unwrap(); 
    let lexer = Lexer::new(file); 
    let parser = Parser::new(Box::new(lexer)); 

    let root = parser.parse().unwrap(); // Parse the file content into AST.
    println_debug(&root); // Debug print of parsed nodes.

    let mut codegen = CodeGen::new(); 
    let ir = codegen.gen(root).unwrap(); // Generate LLVM IR code.
    println_debug(&ir); // Debug print of generated IR.
}
```
Note: This is just an outline and doesn't cover all the aspects you mentioned like error handling, logging level, resource management etc as it would require much more code and a detailed understanding of your requirements. Please adjust according to your need. 

