['The requested library is complex and requires a detailed understanding of real-world requirements. However, it can't be implemented with only a few lines of code because such an implementation would involve thousands of lines of code that don't fit into this platform. It should be developed step by step and following the agile methodology (like Scrum). Below is a simplified skeleton structure for `DataIntegrationFramework`:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public interface IDataSynchronizer<T> where T : class
{
    Task SyncData(IEnumerable<T> data);
}

public class DataIntegrationFramework<T> : IDataSynchronizer<T> where T : class
{
    private readonly List<IDataPipeline> _pipelines;
    private int _currentIndex = 0;

    public DataIntegrationFramework(List<IDataPipeline> pipelines)
    {
        _pipelines = pipelines ?? throw new ArgumentNullException();
    }

    public async Task SyncData(IEnumerable<T> data)
    {
        try
        {
            var tasks = new List<Task>();

            foreach (var pipeline in _pipelines)
            {
                tasks.Add(pipeline.SendAsync(data));
            }

            await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // Log error and switch to next pipeline
            Console.WriteLine($"Error: {ex.Message}");

            if (_currentIndex < _pipelines.Count - 1)
            {
                Interlocked.Increment(ref _currentIndex);
                await SyncData(data);
            }
        }
    }

    //...other methods like Caching, Backpressure etc. would be added here
}

public interface IDataPipeline
{
    Task SendAsync<T>(IEnumerable<T> data) where T : class;
}
```
Please note that this is a very high-level implementation and does not include encryption, distributed caching, backpressure management, external monitoring tools integration, comprehensive security audits, documented risk mitigation strategies, network latency handling etc. As the full scope of these requirements cannot be included in this limited space, they would require a separate detailed design and coding approach.
