4. **Scalability and Concurrent Processing**:
For concurrency control in PHP you can use Swoole, Amp or ReactPHP which provide coroutine-based solutions. Here's an example using Swoole:
```php
\Co\run(function () {
    $ip = '127.0.0.1';
    for($i = 1; $i <= 65535; ++$i) {
        go(function () use ($ip, $i) { // Create a coroutine to handle the connection
            $client = new \Swoole\Coroutine\Client(\SWOOLE_SOCK_TCP);
            if (!$client->connect($ip, $i)) {
                echo "Failed to connect to server.";
                return;
            }
        });
    }
});
```
